#: ../../../AMDGPUInstructionSyntax.md:9
msgid "Syntax of Regular Instructions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUInstructionSyntax.md:11
msgid "An instruction has the following syntax:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUInstructionSyntax.md:13
msgid ""
"`<`*opcode mnemonic*`>    <`*operand0*`>, <`*operand1*`>,...    "
"<`*modifier0*`> <`*modifier1*`>...`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUInstructionSyntax.md:16
msgid ""
"[Operands](AMDGPUOperandSyntax.md) are normally comma-separated, while "
"[modifiers](AMDGPUModifierSyntax.md) are space-separated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUInstructionSyntax.md:19
msgid ""
"The order of *operands* and *modifiers* is fixed. Most *modifiers* are "
"optional and may be omitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUInstructionSyntax.md:22
msgid "Syntax of VOPD Instructions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUInstructionSyntax.md:24
msgid ""
"*VOPDX* and *VOPDY* instructions must be concatenated with the :: operator "
"to form a single *VOPD* instruction:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUInstructionSyntax.md:26
msgid "`<`*VOPDX instruction*`>  ::  <`*VOPDY instruction*`>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUInstructionSyntax.md:28
msgid "An example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AMDGPUInstructionSyntax.md:34
msgid ""
"Note that *VOPDX* and *VOPDY* instructions cannot be used as separate "
"opcodes."
msgstr ""

